  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Caribou is the largest city in Aroostook County, Maine — the northernmost county east of the Mississippi River. With a population of approximately 7,400, Caribou is the commercial hub of the central Aroostook region and serves as the access point for cannabis retail in the St. John Valley and northern Aroostook.</p>
    <p>Per The County's September 2024 reporting on Aroostook's cannabis market, Caribou has two medical cannabis dispensaries — Safe Alternatives on the Presque Isle Road and Richardson's Remedies on the Bog Road (the latter also operates a second location in Presque Isle). Caribou voted to ban retail adult-use marijuana shops within city limits, so there are no adult-use storefronts in town. Adult-use customers travel 15-20 minutes south to Presque Isle, which has become Aroostook's cannabis retail hub.</p>
    <p>Earlier public dispensary directories (Weedmaps, Leafbuyer) listed additional Caribou storefronts. Some of those listings reflect historical operators, incorrectly geocoded addresses (operators physically in Presque Isle but listed under Caribou ZIP code), or pre-ban adult-use storefronts that have since closed. The County's reporting is the most authoritative source on the current medical-vs-adult-use distinction and is used here.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why Caribou's Market Is Medical-Only</h2>
    <p>Several factors explain Caribou's medical-only cannabis market:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Municipal vote.</strong> Per The County, Caribou voted to ban retail marijuana shops within city limits. This was a deliberate opt-out, not a regulatory gap.</li>
      <li><strong>Border geography.</strong> Caribou sits on US Route 1, the main north-south corridor through Aroostook. New Brunswick residents can cross the border for non-cannabis commerce but cannot legally cross with cannabis purchases. The town's cross-border economy doesn't extend to cannabis.</li>
      <li><strong>Adjacent adult-use cluster.</strong> Presque Isle, 15-20 min south, has approved recreational retail and has multiple adult-use dispensaries. Caribou adult-use customers have a short drive to a substantial recreational market, which reduces political pressure for Caribou to opt in.</li>
      <li><strong>Medical operator presence.</strong> Safe Alternatives and Richardson's Remedies are established medical operators serving Aroostook's MMMP patient community. Adult-use licensing would introduce new competitors, which the medical operators may not support.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensary Operators in Caribou</h2>
    <p>Per The County's September 2024 reporting, the medical cannabis dispensary operators in Caribou include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Safe Alternatives</strong> — on the Presque Isle Road. Medical cannabis operator serving Aroostook's MMMP patient community.</li>
      <li><strong>Richardson's Remedies</strong> — on the Bog Road. Also operates a second storefront in Presque Isle (per The County's reporting on Presque Isle as the regional cannabis capital).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Use the Weedmaps Aroostook County directory and the Leafbuyer Aroostook County listings to confirm current addresses, hours, and menus. Operators may have moved or rebranded since The County's September 2024 reporting — verify directly.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>Caribou's medical dispensaries serve a large geographic area across central and northern Aroostook County:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Caribou</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Presque Isle</strong> — 15-20 min south on US Route 1</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Fairfield</strong> — 15 min east (Fort Fairfield banned marijuana businesses altogether per The County)</li>
      <li><strong>Limestone</strong> — 20 min northeast (Loring Air Force Base area)</li>
      <li><strong>Washburn</strong> — 20 min southwest</li>
      <li><strong>Mapleton / Ashland</strong> — 25-35 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Van Buren</strong> — 30 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Madawaska</strong> — 45 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Kent</strong> — 60 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Houlton</strong> (county seat) — 60 min south (Houlton adjusted regulations to keep medical shops only per The County)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For residents of the St. John Valley (Madawaska, Fort Kent, Frenchville, Van Buren), Caribou is the closest medical dispensary cluster. For adult-use shopping, Presque Isle dispensaries serve the same customer base plus Aroostook's broader adult-use population.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Adult-Use vs Medical in Caribou</h2>
    <p>Per The County's reporting, the Caribou market is medical-only at the municipal level. Adult-use customers in Caribou have several options:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Presque Isle (~15-20 min south):</strong> Per The County, Presque Isle "is one of few Aroostook municipalities to approve recreational pot sales" and has become "Aroostook's cannabis capital." Multiple adult-use dispensaries operate there.</li>
      <li><strong>Houlton (~60 min south):</strong> Per The County, Houlton recently adjusted its regulations to keep medical shops only. Not a recreational option.</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Fairfield:</strong> Per The County, banned marijuana businesses altogether.</li>
      <li><strong>Cross-border (New Brunswick):</strong> Not a legal option. Possession and purchase across the international border remains federally illegal for non-Canadians, and Canadian dispensaries don't serve US customers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Confirm each dispensary's specific license framework, hours, and menu with the operator before visiting. Aroostook's cannabis market is shifting — the County's September 2024 reporting is the most authoritative snapshot, but municipal votes can change operator availability.</p>
  </section>

